## SQ-STN-04 | kettle brew time 600 from the default config
@group A
@commands A heated kettle (lit campfire), water tank, one `farmersrespite:black_tea_leaves` in slot 0 and one in slot 1; read `BrewTimeTotal` after 5 ticks. Then `qrun.py toml creativedelight-common.toml cooking.kettleBrewTicks 300`, `/reload`, empty and refill the kettle the same way
@pass First `BrewTimeTotal` 600 and the tea appears at about 600 ticks; after the change 300. The FD pot and the oven still read their own recipe times (an FD pot recipe's `CookTimeTotal` equals the recipe's `cookingtime`)
@fails `KettleRecipeSerializerMixin.ce$cookingTime` fallback; NCH `frBrewing` must not write `cookingtime` (check a dumped recipe json)
@jars creativecommon creativedelight
@sources feature_writeup/remainder_buffer.md
@tier T2
@reviewed 2026-11-20
@from batches/r1106spf/b1.qb
# judge-8 2026-11-21: the 1.19 kettle holds water in its water_level blockstate (no tank NBT); forceload so it ticks
> forceload add 80 -60 80 -60
sleep 3
> setblock 80 -60 -60 minecraft:campfire[lit=true]
> setblock 80 -59 -60 farmersrespite:kettle[water_level=4]
> data merge block 80 -59 -60 {Inventory:{Items:[{Slot:0b,id:"farmersrespite:black_tea_leaves",Count:1b},{Slot:1b,id:"farmersrespite:black_tea_leaves",Count:1b}]}}
sleep 1
> data get block 80 -59 -60
look BrewTimeTotal 600 (kettleBrewTicks default)

## SQ-TP-41 | the Tempad macro (item use path) opens a door and starts the 40-tick cooldown; a second use during it opens nothing
@group A
@commands Bot with a Tempad and 6000 chronons saves a location, pins it, sets the pinned-location macro; `/ztp macro` twice at once, then again after 45 ticks
@pass first macro: a door to the pinned location, `[ztp] cd true`; second macro at once: still one door; after the cooldown: a second door (API opens through `/ztp open` also start the cooldown, owner ruling 2026-11-18, SQ-TP-04)
@fails no cooldown: the macro path does not call the item cooldown (`UseMacroPacket` handler); a second door at once: the cooldown is not checked
@jars creativecompat tempad
@sources feature_writeup/immersive_portals.md feature_writeup/testing/scratch_run_2026-11-07.md
@tier T2
@reviewed 2026-11-18
@absent tempad:default tempad:teleport tempad:pinned_location (Tempad app and macro ids, not registry entries: ModApps / macro ids)
# owner ruling 6 reversed (2026-11-18): both paths start the cooldown; this row checks the macro path (the item-use path a player's shift-use takes)
> forceload add -16 -16 48 16
> pbot spawn t40 0.5 -60 4.5 minecraft:overworld survival
sleep 3
> clear t40
> item replace entity t40 hotbar.0 with tempad:tempad
> ztp setchr t40 0 6000
> tp t40 30.5 -60 4.5 0 0
> ztp save t40 Cool Spot
> tp t40 0.5 -60 4.5 0 0
sleep 2
> ztp pin t40 tempad:default Cool Spot
# judge-8 2026-11-21: the pinned-location macro id is tempad:default (ModMacros.TELEPORT_TO_PINNED)
> ztp settings t40 tempad:teleport tempad:default
> kill @e[type=tempad:timedoor]
sleep 2
> ztp macro t40
> ztp cd t40
waitlog \[ztp\] cd 20
expect \[ztp\] cd true
> ztp macro t40
> ztp doors
waitlog \[ztp\] doors total 20
expect \[ztp\] doors total 1\b
> cdevtest tickwarp 45
waitlog verb=tickwarp end=done 30
> kill @e[type=tempad:timedoor]
> ztp macro t40
> ztp doors
count \[ztp\] door minecraft:overworld .* target minecraft:overworld \(30\.5, -60\.0, 4\.5\) >= 2
> kill @e[type=tempad:timedoor]
> pbot remove t40
reject \[ztp\] (error|unknown subcommand)
reject verb=\S+ .*done=0
look the macro reply lines; the pinned id in the settings reply

## SQ-TP-42 | two chronometers charge the Tempad: the first one found charges, the second is ignored (A4)
@group A
@commands Bot `t42` with a Tempad at 0 chronons in hotbar 0 and two chronometers at 0 in hotbar 1 and 2; `cdevtest tickwarp 2400`; `/ztp chr t42`
@pass the Tempad has chronons after the warp (it was 0 with two chronometers before the fix); the hotbar 2 chronometer still holds 0 (ignored, and `auto_charge_blacklist` keeps it from being charged)
@fails Tempad still 0: `ChronometerItem.isClashing` still stops both (each sees the other in `tempad:chronon_generators`); hotbar 2 above 0: the second chronometer charges itself (first-found check wrong) or is charged by the first (tag missing from the donor)
@jars tempad
@sources development/backportedTempad/PORT_NOTES.md
@tier T2
> pbot spawn t42 0.5 -60 0.5 minecraft:overworld survival
sleep 3
> clear t42
> item replace entity t42 hotbar.0 with tempad:tempad
> item replace entity t42 hotbar.1 with tempad:chronometer
> item replace entity t42 hotbar.2 with tempad:chronometer
> ztp setchr t42 0 0
> cdevtest tickwarp 2400
waitlog verb=tickwarp end=done ticks=2400 120
> ztp chr t42
waitlog \[ztp\] chr end 20
expect \[ztp\] chr slot 0 tempad:tempad [1-9]\d*/
# judge-8 2026-11-21: chronometer capacity 0 (no chronon store, nothing to read); one generator at generation_rate 36 gives about 67 in 2400 ticks, two about 133
expect \[ztp\] chr slot 0 tempad:tempad [1-9]\d?/
> pbot remove t42

