## SQ-IMS-01 | 
@group A
@commands Boot; grep latest.log for `[itemMerges]`
@pass `1 pack merges registered` at startup (woods join after); in the recipe event `pack: 93 merges, N recipes swapped` then `creativedelight: 14 merges, N recipes swapped`, each once; no `already merged`, `already ran`, `chains with` line; no `Error occurred while handling event` from an `item_merges.js`
@fails A group logged twice: the guard keyed on `e.hashCode()` failed; `replaceItems is not a function`: the old Creative Common jar is in `mods/`
@jars creativecommon creativeworldgen
@sources feature_writeup/item_merges.md
@tier T2
@reviewed 2026-11-20
# item_merges.js logs through the startup console; both KubeJS logs are read so the row does not depend on which
shell grep -h "\[itemMerges\]" logs/kubejs/startup.log logs/kubejs/server.log | cut -c1-200
shell grep -qE "\[itemMerges\] [0-9]+ pack merges registered" logs/kubejs/startup.log logs/kubejs/server.log
# r1120lr batch fault: the harness ran a /reload 3 s after Done, so each recipe line showed twice (once per recipe event, correct); the check is now once per recipe event: pack and creativedelight lines equal in number and at least 1
shell p=$(cat logs/kubejs/startup.log logs/kubejs/server.log | grep -cE '\[itemMerges\] pack: [0-9]+ merges, [0-9]+ recipes swapped'); c=$(cat logs/kubejs/startup.log logs/kubejs/server.log | grep -cE '\[itemMerges\] creativedelight: [0-9]+ merges, [0-9]+ recipes swapped'); echo "pack lines $p, creativedelight lines $c"; test "$p" -ge 1 && test "$p" = "$c"
shell ! cat logs/kubejs/startup.log logs/kubejs/server.log | grep -E "\[itemMerges\] .*(already merged|already ran|chains with)"
bootreject Error occurred while handling event.*item_merges|replaceItems is not a function
look the pack and creativedelight merge counts (93 and 14 in the 2026-10-27 build; later merges raise them) and the pack-merges-registered count against item_merges.md

